# README.md is edited by many parallel feature branches, which mostly add
# lines next to each other. The built-in "union" merge driver keeps the
# lines of both sides instead of reporting a conflict. Check the merged
# README for duplicates or wrong order afterwards: union never fails, so
# it never warns either.
#
# Only local git (git merge, git rebase, git pull) honours this. GitHub's
# "Merge pull request" button and its conflict check ignore merge drivers.
README.md merge=union
